<title>JAPAN: Japan 2-year note auction lowest price 99.92.</title>
<headline>Japan 2-year note auction lowest price 99.92.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-02-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>The auction of 120 billion yen in 0.6 percent two-year government notes produced the following results, the Ministry of Finance (MOF) said on Thursday:</p>
<p>Lowest price	 99.92     Stop rate	  0.640 pct</p>
<p>Average price	99.93    Average yield     0.631 pct</p>
<p>Total bids	   308.3 billion yen</p>
<p>Accepted Bids	118.4 billion yen</p>
<p>Bids accepted at lowest price 22.3933 pct</p>
<p>Issue date    March 21, 1997   Maturity    March 22, 1999</p>
<p>Coupon payment     March 20, September 20</p>
</text>
